factcheck by anthropic/claude-haiku-5-5: 5 problems
  The article says the storm will form tomorrow (Monday) and on the 28th will strengthen into a severe storm in the central west Bay of Bengal; the reel_script says it will strengthen on the 28th and move northwest toward the Andhra coast, which is consistent, but the 'அர்னாப் புயல்' naming is fine. However, the reel_script and slides omit the article's note that the storm will become a very severe storm (மிக தீவிர புயல்), a key fact about its intensity.
  The reel_script says the 'Red Alert' applies to 5 districts 'இன்று', and the article says this is for today, which is consistent; but the article's 'Red Alert' also says 'ஓரிரு இடங்களில் இடி மின்னல் மற்றும் பலத்த காற்றுடன் அதி கன மழை' — the reel_script omits the heavy-rain detail for red-alert districts, which is a mismatch in emphasis but not an error.
  The slide 'ஆரஞ்சு அலர்ட்' lists 'மணிக்கு 40 முதல் 50 கிலோமீட்டர் வேகக் காற்று' under the orange alert, but the article attaches that wind speed to the heavy/very heavy rain forecasts, not specifically to the orange-alert districts; this merges two facts from different sentences.
  The slide 'நாளை வானிலை' says Chennai will see 'ஒருசில பகுதிகளில் மிதமான மழை', which matches the article, but the 'அதிகபட்ச வெப்பநிலை 31-32° செல்சியஸ்' is given without the qualifier 'ஒட்டியும்' and the minimum temperature is omitted; this is a loss of accuracy rather than an invention.
  The caption's rainfall line says 'ஓரிரு இடங்களில் இடி மின்னலுடன் அதி கன மழை பெய்யக்கூடும்' generally, while the article ties this to the red-alert districts; the caption's wording is ambiguous about which districts it applies to.
